1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,302
Let's look at Na2O.

2
00:00:02,302 --> 00:00:08,675
Na2O is going to
go 2Na+ plus O2-.

3
00:00:08,675 --> 00:00:09,676
How about alumina?

4
00:00:09,676 --> 00:00:13,079
That's on there, Al2O3.

5
00:00:13,079 --> 00:00:22,255
Well, that's going to
go to 2Al3+ plus 3O2-.

6
00:00:22,255 --> 00:00:25,158
Notice a pattern.

7
00:00:25,158 --> 00:00:26,960
The pattern is you get O2-.

8
00:00:32,232 --> 00:00:35,201
We can understand
why O2- minus has

9
00:00:35,201 --> 00:00:38,638
been used, why
chemistry has been

10
00:00:38,638 --> 00:00:44,344
used to change the properties
of glass for millennia.

11
00:00:44,344 --> 00:00:47,680
And the reason goes
back to the pictures

12
00:00:47,680 --> 00:00:50,050
that we drew on Monday
where we started

13
00:00:50,050 --> 00:00:53,887
by talking about the chemistry
of the silicate group.

14
00:00:53,887 --> 00:00:56,356
So remember Si?

15
00:00:56,356 --> 00:00:58,158
Remember this?

16
00:00:58,158 --> 00:01:04,264
An SiO4 is happy if it's
got four minus charges.

17
